1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,010
Last time, a tadpole grew into a frog.

2
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:06,370
It does not look like the adult, but a chick does.

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:09,510
Then Momo found something strange in the grass!

4
00:00:12,319 --> 00:00:15,369
A little praying mantis is hiding in this video.

5
00:00:15,609 --> 00:00:16,849
Can you spot it?

6
00:00:16,971 --> 00:00:19,071
It is green, and it keeps very still.

7
00:00:19,231 --> 00:00:21,201
Look for two folded front legs!

8
00:00:21,325 --> 00:00:23,165
Lock in first with your fingers.

9
00:00:23,435 --> 00:00:25,265
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:25,852 --> 00:00:27,152
Today you'll learn:

11
00:00:27,357 --> 00:00:28,867
Young that look alike.

12
00:00:29,066 --> 00:00:30,476
What moulting is.

13
00:00:30,675 --> 00:00:32,645
The cockroach's life cycle.

14
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:35,276
Round one.

15
00:00:35,576 --> 00:00:37,916
This little grasshopper has no wings.

16
00:00:38,176 --> 00:00:40,076
Is it the young or the adult?

17
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:41,366
One, the young.

18
00:00:41,676 --> 00:00:42,806
Two, the adult.

19
00:00:43,086 --> 00:00:44,566
Show me with your fingers.

20
00:00:50,039 --> 00:00:51,019
Locked in!

21
00:00:51,147 --> 00:00:51,767
Two!

22
00:00:51,937 --> 00:00:55,077
It has six legs and feelers, like a big grasshopper.

23
00:00:55,297 --> 00:00:56,937
It is just a tiny adult!

24
00:00:57,039 --> 00:01:00,407
One. It is small, with no wings yet, so I think it is

25
00:01:00,427 --> 00:01:01,274
the young.

26
00:01:01,434 --> 00:01:02,154
One!

27
00:01:02,254 --> 00:01:05,764
Grown-up grasshoppers have long wings, and this one has none.

28
00:01:06,714 --> 00:01:07,844
Look closer.

29
00:01:08,454 --> 00:01:11,462
Here is the little grasshopper, beside an adult.

30
00:01:11,482 --> 00:01:15,002
They both have six legs, two feelers, and big back legs for

31
00:01:15,022 --> 00:01:15,824
jumping.

32
00:01:15,844 --> 00:01:18,696
But the adult has long wings, and the little one has none

33
00:01:18,716 --> 00:01:19,339
at all.

34
00:01:19,401 --> 00:01:22,051
A young grasshopper is called a nymph.

35
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:26,571
A nymph looks like the adult, only smaller, and it has no

36
00:01:26,591 --> 00:01:27,571
wings yet.

37
00:01:30,194 --> 00:01:32,144
The answer is one: the young!

38
00:01:32,464 --> 00:01:33,424
One finger?

39
00:01:33,754 --> 00:01:34,944
One finger up!

40
00:01:35,293 --> 00:01:36,593
Say it with me!

41
00:01:37,304 --> 00:01:40,504
The life cycle of a grasshopper has three stages.

42
00:01:40,954 --> 00:01:43,864
The stages are the egg, the young and the adult.

43
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:46,884
The young of the grasshopper is called a nymph.

44
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:51,430
But how does a nymph get its wings?

45
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,710
And look at this.

46
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,000
Did a grasshopper dry up in the sun?

47
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:56,780
Look closer.

48
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,620
It is empty inside, and there is a long split down its

49
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:04,633
back. Even the legs and the feelers are empty, like an old jacket

50
00:02:04,653 --> 00:02:06,171
that somebody took off!

51
00:02:06,191 --> 00:02:08,738
But why would a grasshopper take off its skin?

52
00:02:08,758 --> 00:02:11,758
Its outer skin is hard, and it cannot stretch.

53
00:02:12,338 --> 00:02:15,688
So when the nymph grows, the old skin gets too tight.

54
00:02:18,328 --> 00:02:19,308
Be the nymph!

55
00:02:19,578 --> 00:02:20,568
Shrink down.

56
00:02:20,848 --> 00:02:21,778
Quietly.

57
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:27,017
You are a grasshopper nymph, on a blade of grass.

58
00:02:27,797 --> 00:02:29,857
You munch the leaves, and you grow.

59
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:31,960
Your skin feels tight.

60
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:36,630
You hold on, and your old skin splits open, down your back.

61
00:02:37,138 --> 00:02:40,118
You wriggle out, soft and pale, and a little bigger.

62
00:02:40,898 --> 00:02:43,108
Soon, your new skin turns hard.

63
00:02:43,625 --> 00:02:45,375
You do this several times.

64
00:02:46,145 --> 00:02:48,605
The last time, you come out with wings.

65
00:02:49,385 --> 00:02:50,665
You are an adult!

66
00:02:52,395 --> 00:02:55,805
Shedding the old outer skin to grow bigger has a name.

67
00:02:56,105 --> 00:02:57,585
It is called moulting.

68
00:02:58,825 --> 00:03:01,165
Oops! It did not dry up.

69
00:03:01,255 --> 00:03:03,505
It moulted, and it hopped away bigger!

70
00:03:03,708 --> 00:03:04,858
Say it with me!

71
00:03:05,569 --> 00:03:09,019
As a young insect grows bigger, it sheds its outer skin and

72
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:10,139
grows a new one.

73
00:03:10,909 --> 00:03:12,799
This process is called moulting.

74
00:03:16,425 --> 00:03:17,335
Showdown!

75
00:03:17,635 --> 00:03:18,765
Double points.

76
00:03:19,025 --> 00:03:20,945
Pip's homework has one mistake.

77
00:03:21,225 --> 00:03:23,005
Line one, two, or three?

78
00:03:23,295 --> 00:03:24,765
Show me with your fingers.

79
00:03:24,826 --> 00:03:26,916
My homework is on the cockroach!

80
00:03:27,066 --> 00:03:29,016
One: it has three stages.

81
00:03:29,116 --> 00:03:31,576
Two: its eggs are found in an egg case.

82
00:03:31,766 --> 00:03:34,516
Three: its young does not look like the adult.

83
00:03:40,122 --> 00:03:41,102
Locked in!

84
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:41,970
Three!

85
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:45,620
A cockroach nymph looks like a small adult, only with no wings

86
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,260
yet.

87
00:03:46,314 --> 00:03:46,894
Three.

88
00:03:47,264 --> 00:03:49,234
Only the tadpole looked different.

89
00:03:49,284 --> 00:03:52,314
The chick and the two nymphs all look like their parents.

90
00:03:53,779 --> 00:03:56,139
The young of the cockroach is called a nymph.

91
00:03:57,504 --> 00:03:59,644
Its eggs are found in an egg case.

92
00:04:01,104 --> 00:04:04,054
An egg case is like a tiny brown purse, with lots of

93
00:04:04,074 --> 00:04:05,954
eggs lined up inside!

94
00:04:05,974 --> 00:04:07,064
Three fingers?

95
00:04:07,304 --> 00:04:09,234
Put up two more on your score hand!

96
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:10,824
Say it with us!

97
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:12,785
Egg, young, adult!

98
00:04:13,064 --> 00:04:14,314
Three stages!

99
00:04:17,884 --> 00:04:19,284
Chicks look like hens!

100
00:04:19,464 --> 00:04:20,712
Tadpoles don't!

101
00:04:24,284 --> 00:04:25,533
Skin too tight?

102
00:04:25,864 --> 00:04:27,077
Moult and grow!

103
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:32,909
Show me your score hand!

104
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,239
More than one?

105
00:04:34,539 --> 00:04:35,899
You beat the Buddies.

106
00:04:36,199 --> 00:04:37,259
Three fingers?

107
00:04:37,529 --> 00:04:38,539
High five!

108
00:04:39,044 --> 00:04:40,944
Did you spot the praying mantis?

109
00:04:41,204 --> 00:04:43,654
It was on a sunflower, keeping very still!

110
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:45,100
Here is a fun fact!

111
00:04:45,130 --> 00:04:48,170
The praying mantis is a close cousin of the cockroach.

112
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:51,220
Its eggs are in an egg case too, and lots of tiny

113
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,870
nymphs hatch out together!

114
00:04:52,994 --> 00:04:54,274
Tell someone at home!

115
00:04:55,063 --> 00:04:56,963
Next time: a caterpillar!

116
00:04:57,263 --> 00:04:59,503
One day, it will become a butterfly.

117
00:04:59,783 --> 00:05:02,843
Is the caterpillar a nymph, like the young grasshopper?

118
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:04,213
One, yes.

119
00:05:04,493 --> 00:05:05,343
Two, no.

120
00:05:05,633 --> 00:05:06,943
Lock in your answer!

121
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,420
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:10,470
Ready?

123
00:05:10,757 --> 00:05:11,517
Nymph.

124
00:05:12,762 --> 00:05:13,712
Moulting.

125
00:05:15,149 --> 00:05:16,119
Egg case.

126
00:05:17,506 --> 00:05:18,446
Well done!

127
00:05:19,428 --> 00:05:20,529
Say it with us!

128
00:05:21,329 --> 00:05:22,079
Ready?

129
00:05:22,202 --> 00:05:22,862
One!

130
00:05:23,202 --> 00:05:23,902
two!

131
00:05:24,207 --> 00:05:25,382
Now you know!
